{"title":"Solve for the China tech equilibrium","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/951867911/0/marginalrevolution~Solve-for-the-China-tech-equilibrium.html","date":1774481636000,"content":"<div>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p>Authorities in Beijing have barred two executives from a Singapore-based AI firm from leaving China amid a review of the company’s $2 billion acquisition by U.S. social media giant Meta, according to a report by the Financial Times on Wednesday.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<blockquote>\r\n<p>Xiao Hong and Ji Yichao — the CEO and chief scientist, respectively, of Manus — were summoned to Beijing this month and questioned over a possible violation of foreign direct investment reporting rules related to the acquisition<b> </b>before being told they could not leave the country, the report said.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/03/25/meta-manus-china-executives-banned/\" target=\"_blank\">more from The Washington Post</a>.  In my view, the American lead in AI is somewhat larger than a model comparison alone might suggest.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/03/solve-for-the-china-tech-equilibrium.html\">Solve for the China tech equilibrium</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/951867911/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/951867911/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/951867911/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href